research_rationale:
EO 9245 (7 FR 7328, September 16, 1942; held official Federal Register text) transferred the functions, powers and duties of the United States High Commissioner to the Philippine Islands, with the personnel, records, property and funds of the office, to the Secretary of the Interior. Paragraph 1 of EO 9616 (10 FR 11837, signed September 14, 1945; held Federal Register text) states "Executive Order No. 9245 of Sep­
tember 16, 1942, is hereby repealed" and transfers the same functions, personnel, records, property and funds back from the Secretary of the Interior to the High Commissioner. EO 9616 has no deferred-effect wording, so the transfer to the Secretary ended on 1945-09-14 and the order was not in force on 2026-10-14.
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"Searched the held texts citing EO 9245 by number: only EO 9616 (Federal Register text and two APP transcription files) names it. The order has no sunset or condition. The transfer was made under the First War Powers Act, 1941, but no held source shows that authority or the office ended before 1945-09-14. No earlier end, amendment or partial revocation is held.","independent_command_check":"The order has one command (the transfer of functions, personnel, records, property and funds). It created no body and no separate duty, and the reverse transfer in EO 9616 leaves nothing of EO 9245 in force.","savings_check":"The transfer of functions, personnel, records, property and funds is a completed transfer whose consequences were reversed by paragraph 1 of EO 9616, which returns them to the High Commissioner; the held text of EO 9616 has no separate saving clause. Whatever accrued to the Secretary of the Interior under the 1942 transfer is the subject of the reverse transfer, not of a surviving command under EO 9245.","scope_check":"EO 9245 has a single operative sentence, which paragraph 1 of EO 9616 repeals as a whole by number and date; the repeal is not partial. EO 9616 then re-establishes the transfer in the opposite direction under its own paragraphs 1 to 14, which are new commands of EO 9616."}
